PROMPT 1 — HUSH 0.2 (consolidated)

Goal. Ship HUSH 0.2: persistent sessions + real-time Linux audio engine + general bus routing. Headless only. No GUI, no recording, no MIDI, no plugins, no voice control.

Contracts to lock before coding.

1. Project schema v1 (JSON), stable UUIDs, schema_version = 1, round-trip structural equality.
2. Structured errors: {code, entity_id, message, severity} at every API boundary.
3. Pan law: explicit, project-level, default equal-power −3 dB center; document Soundcraft's ~−4.5 dB as a selectable option.
4. Float contract: internal float32, export 32-bit IEEE float WAV, no dither, no clamping beyond IEEE range.
5. Solo/mute semantics: solo-in-place and channel mute implemented; PFL/AFL and monitor-mute fields reserved in schema.
6. Undo/redo: append-only operation log, invertible, replayable. No snapshots.
7. Real-time graph: preallocated, lock-free parameter queue, lock-free graph swap with documented memory reclamation (pick deferred-free, hazard pointers, or epoch; justify in decision log).
8. Meters: lock-free readout, polled. Xrun/underrun counters exposed.
9. Voice-command pipeline shape reserved in spec. No implementation.

Implementation (in this order).

1. Schema v1 writer/reader + round-trip tests.
2. Operation-log undo/redo + invertibility tests.
3. Autosave (timer + transport-stop) + crash recovery (journal + replay).
4. ALSA backend (JACK/PipeWire as optional compile-time backends, stubbed).
5. Preallocated processing graph + lock-free parameter queue.
6. Lock-free graph swap with documented reclamation.
7. Bus-to-bus routing + hard cycle detection + pre/post sends + insert stubs + meters.
8. Full test suite.

Gates (all must pass in CI).

· Persistence round-trip structural equality.
· Undo-all → redo-all structural equality.
· Kill -9 mid-session → recover → state matches last durable point.
· 60-minute real-time run, 48 kHz / 128 samples, zero xruns on reference Linux box.
· Loopback latency measured in samples and ms.
· Underrun injection → counters correct, no crash.
· Nested-bus render byte-identical to flat-bus render at unity gain.
· 8-hour soak: flat memory, no leaked handles.
· 500 tracks × 200 clips × 20 automation lanes → open/mutate/save/reopen under 2 s.
· All 0.1.0 tests still pass.

Deliverables. Source ZIP (CMake Linux-green, Windows-portable), 0.2 architecture spec, decision log, validation report (with distro/kernel/CPU/ALSA version), honest limitations list, release notes in 0.1.0 format.

Do not ship. GUI, recording, MIDI, plugins, voice control, arrangement, comping, Windows build.

