PROMPT 2 — HUSH 0.3a (mixer GUI)

Goal. Ship a mixer-only native GUI reading from the canonical project model. No arrangement view. No parallel state.

Contracts to lock.

1. GUI reads and writes only through the project-model API. Any direct struct access is a bug.
2. All GUI mutations go through the undo log.
3. Meters are polled from the lock-free readout; never pushed from audio thread.
4. UI toolkit choice (recommend a cross-platform toolkit that survives Windows, e.g. Dear ImGui for engineering builds or Qt for product UI — record the choice and tradeoff in decision log).
5. Layout: channel strips (gain, pan, mute, solo, meter, sends, insert stubs), buses, master. No plugin UIs, no plugin editors.
6. No hidden state — closing and reopening the GUI produces identical view state from the project file.

Implementation.

1. GUI skeleton + project-model binding.
2. Channel strip rendering.
3. Bus and master strips.
4. Send and insert-stub UI.
5. Undo-aware controls (every drag produces one invertible op on release, not one per pixel).
6. CLI/GUI parity test: same mutation via CLI and via GUI produces identical project file.

Gates.

· GUI-vs-CLI parity test passes.
· All 0.2 gates still pass with GUI built.
· 1-hour GUI session, no leaks, no xruns introduced.
· No direct project-model mutation outside the API (enforced by code review + lint rule).

Deliverables. Source ZIP, 0.3a GUI spec, decision log entry for toolkit, validation report, release notes.

Do not ship. Arrangement view, plugin editors, recording, MIDI, voice control.

