PROMPT 3 — HUSH 0.3b (arrangement view)

Goal. Ship the arrangement/timeline view. Read-only playback of existing project state first; editing second.

Contracts to lock.

1. Timeline zoom, scroll, and selection state are view state, not project state — persisted separately as a "view file" beside the project.
2. All timeline edits are undo-log operations, same contract as 0.3a.
3. Clip model: timeline events reference project entities by stable UUID. No parallel clip store.
4. Snapping and grid semantics named explicitly (bar/beat/sample; document grid resolution options).

Implementation.

1. Timeline rendering of tracks, buses, clips (from existing project model).
2. Playhead, transport, follow-playhead.
3. Selection, zoom, scroll.
4. Clip creation/move/trim (undo-logged).
5. View-state persistence.

Gates.

· GUI-vs-CLI parity extended to timeline operations.
· 2-hour session, no leaks, no xruns.
· All prior gates still pass.

Deliverables. Source ZIP, timeline spec, validation report, release notes.

Do not ship. Recording, MIDI editing, comping, plugins, voice.

