PROMPT 4 — HUSH 0.4 (recording, takes, comping, punch)

Goal. Ship multitrack recording, takes/playlists, comping, punch-in/out.

Contracts to lock.

1. Recording writes to disk in a preallocated ring buffer flushed off-thread. No file I/O in the audio callback — recording is exempt from nothing.
2. Take model: each take is a first-class entity with a UUID; a track's "active take" pointer is a project-state field.
3. Playlist model: per-track ordered list of takes; comp is a derived overlay with a UUID.
4. Punch model: punch-in/out points are project-state; pre-roll and post-roll are project-state; recording mode is project-state.
5. Latency compensation contract: input latency measured and reported; user can set compensation offset per device.
6. Crossfade contract: default shape, duration, and boundary rules documented.

Implementation.

1. Ring-buffer recording path + off-thread disk flush.
2. Take capture and playlist assembly.
3. Punch modes (auto-punch, manual punch, loop-record).
4. Comping UI (region-based selection across takes).
5. Crossfades.
6. Latency compensation.

Gates.

· Record 8 tracks × 10 minutes → play back → sample-accurate length and no dropped frames.
· Punch-in/out sample-accurate to ±1 sample.
· Comping: switch active take N times → render comparison bit-identical to manually assembled reference.
· Latency loopback measurement reported and stable across sessions.
· All prior gates pass.

Deliverables. Source ZIP, recording spec, validation report, release notes, expanded limitations list.

Do not ship. MIDI, plugins, voice.

