PROMPT 6 — HUSH 0.6 (VST3 plugin hosting)

Goal. Ship VST3 hosting on Linux and prepare Windows. No CLAP, no AU in this milestone.

Contracts to lock.

1. Plugin processes out-of-process by default (sandboxed host process). In-process is an opt-in for trusted plugins. Record the tradeoff (stability vs. latency/CPU) in the decision log.
2. Plugin state is part of the project state, saved/restored per instance.
3. Plugin failures (crash, hang) must not take down the engine — sandbox restart with a structured error.
4. Latency reporting: plugin latency reported and compensated automatically; user-visible.
5. Scan safety: plugin scan runs in a sandbox with a watchdog.
6. Insert model: previous "stub" points become real insert points; schema bump to schema_version = 2 with a migration from v1.

Implementation.

1. VST3 SDK integration on Linux.
2. Out-of-process host process + IPC contract.
3. Sandbox crash/hang handling.
4. Plugin scanning UI and safety.
5. Insert points activated on tracks, buses, master.
6. Plugin editors (embed in sandbox window).
7. Latency compensation integration.
8. Schema v2 migration from v1.

Gates.

· Load 50 plugins across 20 tracks → engine runs 60 minutes, zero xruns.
· Kill a plugin process mid-session → engine survives, project state consistent, structured error logged.
· Plugin-state round-trip: save project with plugin states → reload → bit-identical render.
· Schema v1 project opens under v2 with migration and renders identically to pre-migration.
· All prior gates pass.

Deliverables. Source ZIP, plugin-hosting spec, sandbox IPC spec, schema v2 migration doc, validation report, release notes.

Do not ship. CLAP, AU, Windows-specific hosting, voice.

