PROMPT 7 — HUSH 0.7 (Windows parity)

Goal. Ship a Windows build at feature parity with Linux. No new features; this milestone is port and parity only.

Contracts to lock.

1. No Win32-specific code in the engine. All OS differences behind interfaces (device backend, file I/O, threading, IPC).
2. Windows device backend choice recorded (WASAPI exclusive/shared, ASIO optional) with tradeoffs.
3. Cross-platform file format: project schema v2 loads and saves identically on both platforms; render comparisons must be bit-identical cross-platform for identical inputs.
4. Build system: CMake presets for both platforms; CI matrix (Linux + Windows).
5. File paths, line endings, and case-sensitivity handled explicitly.

Implementation.

1. Windows device backend.
2. Windows IPC for plugin sandbox.
3. Windows file I/O interface.
4. Windows threading abstractions.
5. CMake presets + CI matrix.
6. Installer (recommend WiX or Inno Setup; record choice).

Gates.

· Full test suite green on Windows in CI.
· Cross-platform render comparison: same project → bit-identical output on Linux and Windows.
· Plugin sandbox works on Windows with the same crash/hang survival semantics.
· All prior gates pass on both platforms.
· Installer produces a working install.

Deliverables. Source ZIP, Windows build instructions, CI config, cross-platform parity report, release notes.

Do not ship. macOS (deferred to 1.0), voice.

