PROMPT 8 — HUSH 0.8 (automation + interchange)

Goal. Ship full automation, harden undo, and ship first session-interchange converters.

Contracts to lock.

1. Automation is a first-class project entity (UUID), on any track/bus/master parameter, with curve types (linear, exponential, S-curve) and modes (read, touch, latch, write).
2. Undo log size budget: document growth rate and compaction policy; no unbounded memory.
3. Interchange scope: AAF and OMF in, REAPER .RPP in (best-effort, lossily documented), AAF out. Pro Tools .ptx and Ableton .als are out of scope (no public spec).
4. Interchange guarantees documented per converter: what round-trips losslessly, what warns, what refuses.

Implementation.

1. Automation entity + editing UI + curve types + modes.
2. Undo-log compaction + stress test.
3. AAF/OMF import.
4. REAPER .RPP import with documented fidelity.
5. AAF export.

Gates.

· Automation render comparison: 20 automated parameters → render bit-identical to hand-authored reference.
· Undo log compaction: 10,000 operations → memory flat after compaction, no loss of undo history within budget.
· AAF round-trip within HUSH: export → import → render bit-identical.
· .RPP import on a corpus of 10 reference projects: documented fidelity report, no crashes.
· All prior gates pass.

Deliverables. Source ZIP, automation spec, interchange fidelity report per converter, validation report, release notes.

Do not ship. Pro Tools/Ableton import, voice.

