PROMPT 9 — HUSH 0.9 (voice + AOC Magic)

Goal. Ship HUSH voice control with AOC Magic safety gates.

Contracts to lock.

1. Pipeline: parser → intent → authorization → preview/confirm → execute → audit log. Every stage is a distinct module with a testable interface.
2. Destructive operations require explicit confirmation. "Delete tracks," "overwrite takes," "clear automation" — all gated.
3. Every voice action is undo-logged and is a normal project operation. Voice has no privileged path.
4. Audit log is append-only, separate from the undo log, and records: intent, resolved action, confirmation, result, timestamp.
5. Voice intent taxonomy documented: at minimum track creation/deletion, arm/disarm, transport control, bus creation, send creation, comp assembly, scene launch.
6. No voice command may bypass the preview step. Even non-destructive commands are previewed (with the option to "confirm and don't preview again for this command type," stored per project).
7. Fail-closed: if intent is ambiguous, refuse and ask.

Implementation.

1. Parser (grammar spec + tests).
2. Intent resolver against the project model.
3. Authorization module.
4. Preview UI (in mixer and arrangement views).
5. Confirmation flow.
6. Audit log.
7. Intent taxonomy implementation for §5 list.

Gates.

· Every voice intent in the taxonomy has a passing end-to-end test.
· Destructive command without confirmation → refused, audit-logged.
· Every executed voice command produces an undo-log entry invertible by the same undo system as GUI/CLI.
· Fuzz test: 1,000 malformed commands → no crash, all fail-closed.
· Ambiguous command → refuse + structured prompt, not guess.
· All prior gates pass.

Deliverables. Source ZIP, voice/AOC spec, intent taxonomy doc, audit-log format doc, validation report, release notes.

Do not ship. 1.0 marketing claims, macOS, Pro Tools/Ableton import.

